From d7059dc0d609c8a3ff661b0b72529a3bb85dd89d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 04:42:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [GBM][GLES] GUI composite: a mode into SDR of BT.2020
 primaries

An SDR video of BT.2020 primaries can only go out as it is if what Kodi
draws over it, the GUI and the subtitles, is in BT.2020 too: they are made
in sRGB, of BT.709 primaries, and a display told BT.2020 shows them too
saturated (the yellow of subtitles drawn towards green). The composite of
the GUI that HDR uses (the GUI drawn into an FBO and converted over the
picture by gles_gui_composite.frag) only knew PQ and HLG.

Its SDR mode (CGuiCompositeShaderGLES::SDR_BT2020, u_sdrWide) converts as
ITU-R BT.2087 case #1 does, to keep the colours that a BT.709 display shows:
the non-linear signal to linear light by the reference EOTF of ITU-R BT.1886
(2.40, black 0), the BT.709 to BT.2020 matrix, and back by its inverse.
Every grey stays the same code. The FBO holds the GUI premultiplied by its
coverage: that is divided out before the conversion, and the result is
mixed over the picture by the coverage, as Kodi mixes the GUI in SDR (not
by its square, which the composite into PQ and HLG uses). The mode needs
highp in fragment shaders (KODI_GUI_EXACT); without it, it is not set up.

IsHdrComposite() stays true for PQ and HLG only: the overlays that are
already in PQ, drawn straight onto the picture, and their range are HDR
things. The new IsGuiComposite() is true for any composite, and is what the
coverage of the GUI in the FBO (CGUITextureGLES::DrawQuad()), the range of
the GUI shaders (the composite encodes it) and the transparent clear of the
slideshow over a video ask for. The packer of native Dolby Vision output
does not take the SDR mode for PQ (IsPQ()), the GUI white of HDR does not
apply to it, a hand-over to native Dolby Vision sets the composite into PQ
again, the line of the composite every 10 seconds names it, and the
window's buffer is cleared to the black of limited range where the mode
encodes that range, as Kodi draws the bars of SDR video there.

The composite into PQ and HLG draws the same bytes as before: the shader of
the base and this one gave the same pixels on Mesa's llvmpipe for PQ, PQ
with another GUI white, HLG and limited range, at 8 and 10 bits.
